      "quote": "'Cause I'm working seven acres of quiet ground\nWhile they got seven skies burning, tearing it all down\nI'm trying to grow a root in the muddy clay\nWhile the architects of ash blow the world away",
      "story": "Track 3, \"Seven Skies Burning,\" directly contrasts the protagonist's life-giving work on his seven-acre farm with the empire's death-dealing endless wars. It explores the cognitive dissonance of trying to nurture a closed-loop system of survival in the dirt while the ruling class profits from setting the rest of the world on fire. It positions the act of growing food and tending the soil as a quiet, grounded rebellion against a centralized machine obsessed with destruction and debt.\n\nDark acoustic guitar, heavy kick drum, distorted cello\n\n16:9 hyper-realistic split-focus image. In the sharp foreground, a pair of worn hands gently plants a vibrant green seedling into rich soil. In the blurred background, an apocalyptic sky churns with dark smoke and fiery orange flames.\n\n[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nI pull my boots on before the morning breaks\nWalk the fence line just to see what it takes\nGot a handful of seeds and a bucket of rain\nTrying to coax a little life from this Maple Valley pain\nThe soil is heavy, the work is slow\nBut it's the only honest truth that I know\n[Chorus]\n'Cause I'm working seven acres of quiet ground\nWhile they got seven skies burning, tearing it all down\nI'm trying to grow a root in the muddy clay\nWhile the architects of ash blow the world away\nYeah, I'm pulling up the weeds in the morning light\nWhile the suits in the city buy another endless fight\n[Verse 2]\nThere's a Trillion dollar budget for a desert campaign\nA boardroom clapping for the missiles that rain\nThey don't know the smell of the earth when it's turned\nThey only know the profit when the whole thing is burned\nThey send the hometown boys to the fire and the sand\nAnd leave 'em begging for a peach from a neighbor's hand\n[Chorus]\n'Cause I'm working seven acres of quiet ground\nWhile they got seven skies burning, tearing it all down\nI'm trying to grow a root in the muddy clay\nWhile the architects of ash blow the world away\nYeah, I'm pulling up the weeds in the morning light\nWhile the suits in the city buy another endless fight\n[Bridge]\nYou can't eat the ledger!\nYou can't drink the oil!\nThe only truth left... is the blood in the soil.\n\n[Outro]\nLet the skies burn.\nI'll tend the dirt.\nLet the high towers hum.\nI know exactly where it hurts.\nJust seven acres.\n\u00a9 2026 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
