      "story": "Track 9, \"Stock Ticker Lullaby,\" opens Act III by shifting the focus from the domestic tragedies of Act II to the corporate beneficiaries of those tragedies. It explores how the military-industrial complex profits from endless conflict, specifically tracking the soaring stock valuations of defense conglomerates like Lockheed Martin and RTX following the initiation of new wars. With a cynical, slightly industrial-leaning acoustic arrangement, this track serves as a cold, systemic indictment of an economy where the blood of the working class is converted directly into shareholder dividends.\n\nHeavy industrial stomp, percussive acoustic guitar slapping, dissonant slide guitar\n\n16:9 dark composition. A highly polished brass artillery shell stands upright. Spiraling tightly around it is a stream of glossy white stock ticker tape printed with glowing green arrows. The blurred background reveals a dark Wall Street trading floor.\n\n[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nThere's a bell ringing loud on the trading floor\nWhile the boots hit the sand in a brand new war\nThe anchor on the screen got a tear in his eye\nWhile the blue-chip brokers watch the margins fly\nFour million dollars for a single flame\nJust a line on a ledger in an infinite game\n[Chorus]\nSing a stock ticker lullaby, watch the arrows rise\nGreen numbers flashing in the hollow men's eyes\nEvery time a hometown boy goes down in the dirt\nAnother dividend is paid to the ones who never hurt\nYeah, the L.M.T. and the R.T.X.\nCashing in the blood on the latest checks.\nJust a stock ticker lullaby.\n[Verse 2]\nThey sit in the boardroom drinking top-shelf wine\nWhile the infantry holds the unapproved line\nThey don't hear the thunder, they don't feel the heat\nThey just track the returns from a penthouse suite\nA multi-billion contract for the fire in the sky\nWhile the folks back home are just waving goodbye\n[Chorus]\nSing a stock ticker lullaby, watch the arrows rise\nGreen numbers flashing in the hollow men's eyes\nEvery time a hometown boy goes down in the dirt\nAnother dividend is paid to the ones who never hurt\nYeah, the L.M.T. and the R.T.X.\nCashing in the blood on the latest checks.\nJust a stock ticker lullaby.\n[Bridge]\nThe market always responds well to a crisis.\nEspecially when you're the one manufacturing it.\nBuy the rumor!\nSell the blood!\n\n[Outro]\nWatch the arrows rise.\nCashing the checks.\nMarket closes at four.\n\u00a9 2026 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
