      "quote": "It's the unapproved war, flying under the night\nNo hands raised up in the morning light\nThey bypassed the gavel and they buried the law\nFeeding the belly of the unapproved war",
      "story": "Track 10, \"The Unapproved War,\" tackles the systemic death of the democratic process regarding military intervention. The song focuses on how the executive branch and defense apparatus continuously bypass Congressional approval, launching unilateral military actions without the consent of the governed. It channels the frustration of a working-class public whose sons, daughters, and tax dollars are committed to endless conflicts drafted behind closed doors, turning the Constitution into a \"ghost in the hall.\"\n\nDriving acoustic guitar strumming, heavy marching snare drum, distorted electric guitar\n\n16:9 low-angle cinematic shot. An old, heavy wooden judge's gavel lies cracked and abandoned on the dusty floor of a dark marble hallway. A single, harsh beam of light cuts across the scene to illuminate the broken wood.\n\n[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nThey locked the heavy doors on the chamber hall\nNo debate on the floor, no roll call\nA quiet little whisper and a stroke of the pen\nAnd they\u2019re sending out the hometown boys again\nThere was no declaration for the people to see\nJust a late-night memo and a shadow decree\n[Chorus]\nIt's the unapproved war, flying under the night\nNo hands raised up in the morning light\nThey bypassed the gavel and they buried the law\nFeeding the belly of the unapproved war\nYeah, the people didn't speak, but the people will pay\nFor the unapproved war at the end of the day.\n[Verse 2]\nMillions of dollars moving over the wire\nTo throw a little fuel on an endless fire\nThe Constitution is a ghost in the marble hall\nWhile the executives rise and the young men fall\nThey wrap up the treason in a security brief\nAnd leave the working man alone with the grief\n[Chorus]\nIt's the unapproved war, flying under the night\nNo hands raised up in the morning light\nThey bypassed the gavel and they buried the law\nFeeding the belly of the unapproved war\nYeah, the people didn't speak, but the people will pay\nFor the unapproved war at the end of the day.\n[Bridge]\nThe loudest sound in the capital...\nIs the silence of the vote.\nThey took the voice of the people!\nAnd shoved it down our throat!\n\n[Outro]\nNo declaration.\nNo consent.\nJust the unapproved war.\n\u00a9 2026 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
