      "quote": "So pass the hat around for the hometown crew\nWhen the government fails, it comes down to you\nWe don't need a ledger, we don't need a king\nWe just need the shelter that a neighbor can bring",
      "story": "Track 14, \"Pass the Hat,\" re-contextualizes the tragedy of Track 8 (the food drive) into a triumph of local solidarity. It shifts the focus away from the failure of the government and instead celebrates the everyday heroes\u2014the local mental health workers, sisters-in-law, and neighbors\u2014who actually step up to care for the vulnerable when the state fails. It serves as an uplifting, rhythmic folk song that honors the true, hidden safety net of the nation.\n\nFast energetic acoustic guitar strumming, upbeat tambourine, bright soaring fiddle\n\n16:9 uplifting image. A faded canvas working man's cap is held out by calloused hands. Inside, hands of different ages and races drop in crumpled dollar bills, fresh garden vegetables, and a shiny silver wrench. Bright, communal lighting.\n\n[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nMy sister-in-law is working the county line\nA mental health worker working on borrowed time\nShe\u2019s taking the calls from the boys who are falling apart\nStitching together the pieces of a broken heart\nThe federal budget forgot 'em and left 'em to fade\nBut she\u2019s out in the trenches, standing right in the shade\n[Chorus]\nSo pass the hat around for the hometown crew\nWhen the government fails, it comes down to you\nWe don't need a ledger, we don't need a king\nWe just need the shelter that a neighbor can bring\nYeah, the empire is hollow and the promises flat\nBut the people survive when they pass the hat!\nPass it around!\n[Verse 2]\nDown at the drive-through pantry in the pouring rain\nA hundred old engines idling in the lane\nBut look at the hands that are handing the boxes of bread\nIt ain't the politicians making sure they are fed\nIt's the mechanic, the teacher, the guy from the mill\nPaying the balance of a broken-down bill\n[Chorus]\nSo pass the hat around for the hometown crew\nWhen the government fails, it comes down to you\nWe don't need a ledger, we don't need a king\nWe just need the shelter that a neighbor can bring\nYeah, the empire is hollow and the promises flat\nBut the people survive when they pass the hat!\nPass it around!\n[Bridge]\nThey can keep their gold curtains!\nThey can keep their high towers!\nBecause the dirt and the roots...\nAre entirely ours!\n\n[Outro]\nPass the hat!\nTake care of your own!\nPass the hat!\nYou ain't alone!\n\u00a9 2026 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
